# Which packages a NixOS node gets, by role: plain data, read by the IPS
# (lib/functions.d/node-bundle-functions.sh, node_role_packages) when a starter
# node asks for its package list (boot_manager.sh cmd=node_packages).
#
# One line per role:   ROLE: name name ...
# ROLE is a word of the host's registry TYPE (SCH, TCH, ...); the role * is every
# node. A host of TYPE SCH,TCH gets both lines. Each name is a NAME of
# lib/starter/nixos.packages, resolved to a store path through the repository's
# manifest (hps-starter sync nixos), so a name the package list lacks is an error
# the node reports, not a package that is silently left out.
#
# ZFS is already in the stock starter and is not listed. The lines below carry what
# the storage and compute scripts call (docs/BUNDLE.md "Storage and compute"); a
# package added to a line arrives on a running node at its next bundle-refresh.

# The ctrl-exec agent and its executor (a local package: its closure carries perl, its modules and openssl).
*: ctrl-exec-agent

# Storage controller: the iSCSI target, md, SMART, the key converter (xxd), om3 and the log forwarder.
SCH: targetcli-fb mdadm smartmontools xxd jq rsyslog om3

# Compute host: libvirt and QEMU (with all the display and audio libraries the
# stock qemu-host-cpu-only closure carries: headless QEMU is plan step 5), the
# iSCSI initiator, md mirrors, frame capture, om3 and the log forwarder.
TCH: libvirt qemu-host-cpu-only open-iscsi mdadm tcpdump jq rsyslog om3
